{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Align the helper's change/patchset validation with the sibling comment step's `^[1-9][0-9]*$` (ASCII-only) semantics rather than `str.isdecimal()`.","criteria":["correctness","maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py:32: `if not value.isdecimal() or value.startswith(\"0\"):`",".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:594: `if [[ ! \"${CHANGE_NUMBER}\" =~ ^[1-9][0-9]*$ ]]; then`","Comment on ticket/description says validation should mirror 'the existing cast/comment boundary' but the sibling ASCII-only regex and the Python isdecimal() check are not equivalent for Unicode decimal digits."],"finding":"The helper's positive-integer validation `value.isdecimal() and not value.startswith('0')` diverges from the sibling comment step's stricter regex `^[1-9][0-9]*$`. `str.isdecimal()` returns True for non-ASCII Unicode decimal digits (e.g. Arabic-Indic '٢'), so a Unicode-digit CHANGE_NUMBER/PATCHSET_NUMBER passes validation in the helper but would be rejected by the sibling step and produces a malformed Gerrit change ref.","id":"0","impact":0.27,"location":"scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py:31","norm_id":"nb906781fb1cfd33a","priority":0.2025,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"suggested_fix":"Validate with a compiled `re.fullmatch(r\"[1-9][0-9]*\", value)` so the helper and the sibling shell step enforce identical ASCII-only positive-integer semantics.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":true,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.5,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Tighten the closed-change classifier to match Gerrit's error line specifically (e.g. anchored to a stderr line) rather than a bare substring of merged stdout+stderr.","criteria":["error-handling"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py:50: `return _CLOSED_CHANGE_NEEDLE in f\"{completed.stderr}\\n{completed.stdout}\"`","scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py:111: `if completed.returncode != 0 and _is_closed_change_error(completed):`","The guard is gated on returncode != 0 and only downgrades a specific string, so genuinely unrelated failures (e.g. ssh 255 host-key errors) still fail closed; the residual concern is only that the needle is a plain substring of merged output."],"finding":"The closed-change classifier matches the needle against combined stderr+stdout for ANY nonzero return, but does not require that the Gerrit review command actually ran to co